"use strict";(self.webpackChunk_N_E=self.webpackChunk_N_E||[]).push([[5702],{75702:e=>{e.exports=JSON.parse('{"slug":"eksport-dizelya-oktyabr-2026-dempfer-ceny","locale":"en","title":"Russia partly reopens diesel exports as winter diesel reaches another exchange-price record","description":"Russia partly permitted diesel exports from October 10, 2026, with an initial 500 thousand tonnes. How the fuel compensation mechanism works and what domestic diesel prices may face.","blocks":[{"id":"b001","kind":"paragraph","text":"On October 9, 2026, the US Treasury issued a license permitting transactions involving Russian diesel until April 7, 2027. From October 10, the Russian government partly lifted the export ban that had applied to all producers since July. The initial stage covers 500 thousand tonnes, with exports subject to quotas and government approval. That is about 29% of the volume previously exported by pipeline in a month. The gasoline export ban remains in force until January 31, 2027."},{"id":"b002","kind":"paragraph","text":"Diesel is scarce worldwide. On October 14, the International Energy Agency estimated that global diesel exports in September had fallen by 700 thousand barrels a day from a year earlier: Russia and the Middle East lost 1.3 million barrels a day, and other suppliers replaced only part of that volume. The agency expects inventories to recover no earlier than the second half of 2027. Russia\'s 500 thousand tonnes represent about 3.7 million barrels, less than 1% of monthly global consumption. Even the entire 4.8 million tonnes mentioned by Donald Trump would cover only a little more than 1 day of world demand, so global prices are unlikely to move substantially."},{"id":"b003","kind":"paragraph","text":"Diesel is cheaper within Russia. In September, an export tonne cost 147 268 rubles, versus a domestic wholesale price of 67.73 thousand. Compensation is calculated not against the actual domestic price but a notional price of 58 950 rubles. Imagine a farmer who can sell milk to a neighbor for 59 rubles or in the city for 147. To keep the milk in the village, the local council pays part of the difference. Fuel works similarly: the budget compensates oil companies for 65% of the gap, about 57 thousand rubles per tonne. This is the fuel price compensation mechanism, or damper. September payments reached 305.5 billion rubles, the highest since April 2022. Including other deductions, oil companies received back 418.5 billion, or 48% of all oil and gas taxes."},{"id":"b004","kind":"paragraph","text":"The mechanism has a threshold. If the monthly average wholesale diesel price exceeds 76.63 thousand rubles per tonne, payments fall to zero. The monthly average matters, not a single spike: it reached 75.07 thousand in August and fell to 67.73 thousand in September. Yet winter diesel set a record of 81.8 thousand on October 8. The planned exports are summer fuel, which is in surplus domestically, whereas winter fuel is becoming more expensive as cold weather approaches and supply is short. Without compensation, selling abroad would become even more attractive, so officials are discussing a moratorium on zeroing the payments. Deputy Prime Minister Alexander Novak says exports will not affect Russian consumers."},{"id":"b005","kind":"paragraph","text":"Exports benefit the budget. Finance Minister Anton Siluanov expects oil companies\' revenue to support the balance of payments and generate taxes on their profits. Each tonne sold abroad requires no payment under the domestic fuel compensation mechanism."},{"id":"b006","kind":"paragraph","text":"While quotas are small and compensation continues, drivers will barely notice the exports at filling stations. However, the budget will keep compensating oil companies; in September this amounted to almost half of oil and gas taxes. A worse outcome for drivers would be a monthly average diesel price above the threshold without a moratorium: oil companies would then have a stronger incentive to export, and domestic diesel could become more expensive."},{"id":"b007","kind":"heading","text":"Why did Russia permit diesel exports in October 2026?"},{"id":"b008","kind":"paragraph","text":"On October 9 the US Treasury issued a license permitting Russian diesel transactions until April 7, 2027. From October 10 the Russian government partly lifted the export ban: the initial stage is 500 thousand tonnes, subject to quotas and government approval. Deputy Prime Minister Alexander Novak says the domestic market will be fully supplied."},{"id":"b009","kind":"heading","text":"What is the fuel price compensation mechanism?"},{"id":"b010","kind":"paragraph","text":"It is a budget payment to oil companies for selling fuel domestically for less than they could receive abroad. In September 2026, the budget compensated 65% of the difference between an export price of about 147 thousand rubles per tonne and a notional domestic price of about 59 thousand. Total September payments under the mechanism were 305.5 billion rubles."},{"id":"b011","kind":"heading","text":"Will diesel become more expensive in Russia because of exports?"},{"id":"b012","kind":"paragraph","text":"Export volumes are small, initially 500 thousand tonnes, and subject to quotas. The risk lies elsewhere. Winter diesel reached an exchange-price record of 81.8 thousand rubles per tonne on October 8, above the 76.6 thousand threshold. If the monthly average diesel price exceeds that threshold, compensation falls to zero and exporting becomes even more attractive. Officials are therefore discussing a moratorium on zeroing payments."}],"sources":[{"label":"Government partly lifts diesel export ban","url":"https://www.tut-news.ru/ekonomika/kabmin-chastichno-snyal-zapret-na-eksport-dizelya"},{"label":"An act of relief","url":"https://www.kommersant.ru/doc/9023946"},{"label":"Keeping domestic supplies intact: which diesel Russia will send to Trump","url":"https://aif.ru/money/economy/ot-sebya-ne-otorvem-kakoe-dizelnoe-toplivo-rossiya-otpravit-trampu"},{"label":"Oil companies received back almost half their September taxes as a subsidy to contain fuel prices","url":"https://ru.themoscowtimes.com/2026/10/05/neftyaniki-vsentyabre-poluchili-obratno-pochti-polovinu-svoih-nalogov-vkachestve-subsidii-nasderzhivanie-tsen-natoplivo-a207832"},{"label":"Winter diesel reaches another exchange-price record","url":"https://finance.mail.ru/article/zimnij-dizel-na-birzhe-obnovil-rekord-69231538/"},{"label":"Siluanov explains Russia\'s benefit from the diesel deal with the US","url":"https://lenta.ru/news/2026/10/13/siluanov-ob-yasnil-vygodu-rossii-ot-dizelnoy-sdelki-s-ssha"},{"label":"Trump\'s diesel deal with Russia unlikely to significantly reduce fuel prices","url":"https://www.cnbc.com/2026/10/13/trump-putin-zelenskyy-russia-ukraine-diesel-oil-price.html"},{"label":"IEA warns diesel market will stay tight into second half of 2027","url":"https://www.cnbc.com/2026/10/14/diesel-deal-oil-price-iea-report.html"}],"sourceBodySha256":"4d6c93f6a2b442a1c062b486b428a7b0cfc11a60a49fbe0f2cc57b3fdc9ff699"}')}}]);